    {
      "text": "those who reject prophets have strayed from ordinances, broken everlasting covenant, D&C 1:15. those who have received revelation may fall if they follow own will, D&C 3:4. because of transgression, if thou art not aware thou wilt fall, D&C 3:9–11. if Martin Harris does not humble himself and receive witness, he will fall into transgression, D&C 5:32. Satan causes men to catch themselves in own snare, D&C 10:26. wo unto him who denies revelation, D&C 11:25. Book of Mormon contains record of fallen people, D&C 20:9. possibility that man may fall from grace, D&C 20:32. fear of persecution and cares of world cause James Covel to reject word, D&C 40:2. he who builds upon this rock shall never fall, D&C 50:44. if he repent not of his sins, let him take heed lest he fall, D&C 58:15. he who sins against greater light receives greater condemnation, D&C 82:3. those who sin against covenant are delivered to buffetings of Satan, D&C 82:21. whoso breaks covenant shall not have forgiveness, D&C 84:41. minds darkened because of unbelief, D&C 84:54. those who have apostatized shall have no inheritance among Saints, D&C 85:11. Satan sows tares, D&C 86:3. some have blasphemed against the Lord in midst of his house, D&C 112:26. some among Saints deny the Lord’s name, D&C 114:2. let men be appointed to supply place of those who are fallen, D&C 118:1. amen to priesthood of those who cover their sins, D&C 121:37.",
